<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n12113" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">cȳcnēus</span></b>  (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">cȳgn-</span></b> ), a,
		um, adj., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κύκνειος</span>. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>Of</i> or <i>belonging to a swan,
				swan's-</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">tamquam cycnea vox et oratio,</span>”
				i. e. <i>the last speech</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					de Or. 3, 2, 6</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">plumae,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ov.
					Tr. 4, 8, 1</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Cȳcnēa</span></b>  (al.
				 Cygnaea) Specula, <i>a hill near
				Brixia</i>, now still <i>Cigneo</i>, <i><span class="en">Cat. 67,
			32</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
